{"Title":"An Act relative to dependent eligibility for Chapter 115 benefits","BillNumber":"S2347","DocketNumber":"SD599","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"MFR0","Name":"Michael F. Rush","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MFR0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T15:08:09.31"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"MFR0","Name":"Michael F. Rush","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MFR0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T15:08:09.31"},{"Id":"P_M1","Name":"Paul McMurtry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/P_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-08T12:47:18.9366667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2347/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Rush, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2347) of Michael F. Rush and Paul McMurtry for legislation relative to dependent eligibility for Chapter 115 benefits.  Veterans and Federal Affairs.","DocumentText":"\tSection 1 of Chapter 115 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended in line 18, by inserting after the words “carried on” the following:-  \r\n\t“Dependents of Veterans who meet all eligibility criteria except for the one day residence in the commonwealth, shall be eligible for benefits under this chapter provided a dependent provides proof of residency in Massachusetts for no less than one year prior to application of benefits.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J31","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J31"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}